WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.160
Hi everyone!
Thanks for tuning in to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:08.880
our third and final video on this English Online&nbsp;
Business English series for building resilience.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:11.600
Let’s take a look at our third tip.

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.960
This is something that might sound like&nbsp;
a little bit of a cliché, but it is much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:23.600
harder to put into practice than you might&nbsp;
think, and that is being kind to yourself.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:30.480
I know for me, I am my own harshest critic.
I always set the bar for myself way higher than I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:36.720
would expect anyone else in my position to achieve&nbsp;
or to reach and I know I’m not the only one.

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:42.160
Being kind to yourself is not only&nbsp;
about reducing our negative self-talk,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:47.440
but is also about taking care of&nbsp;
ourselves both physically and mentally.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.760
Let’s take a look at five tips&nbsp;
that you could apply to your life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:57.280
over the next few weeks, and see if it&nbsp;
makes a difference to your resilience.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:03.120
Our first tip might seem like a little bit of an&nbsp;
easy one, but trust me, it makes a big difference.&nbsp;

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:07.440
If you don’t already, you should&nbsp;
start making your bed in the morning.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:12.080
Making our bed in the morning really sets us up&nbsp;
for the day and makes us feel like, that we’ve&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.920
already achieved something, even though it’s&nbsp;
super small, and it helps you to feel prepared.

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:23.200
Our second tip is about exercise.&nbsp;
I know this isn’t always possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:27.040
so you could also think of it&nbsp;
this way. The two-minute rule.&nbsp;

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:32.320
If I’m lacking in energy, feeling down, or&nbsp;
just not in the mood, do it for two minutes.&nbsp;

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:39.840
The chances are, once you’ve started, you will do&nbsp;
it for a little bit longer than the two minutes.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:43.680
And, if you’ve started, you’ve done your two&nbsp;
minutes and you really can’t be bothered to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:48.800
keep going, then don’t, stop. You did&nbsp;
it for two minutes, try again tomorrow.

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:53.600
Our third tip is to avoid toxic positivity.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:02:00.880
Recently, there has been a huge growth in the area&nbsp;
of self-care and mindfulness which is amazing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:08.000
but don’t forget that it is also okay to&nbsp;
have a bad day, or to be in a terrible mood.&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.360
You don’t have to be positive&nbsp;
and happy all the time.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:16.720
Our next tip, don’t forget to take stock of&nbsp;
all the things that you have actually achieved.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:22.000
Recently I had a conversation with a friend&nbsp;
of mine who was feeling a little bit down.&nbsp;

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:25.120
She was talking about some new&nbsp;
colleagues that she had met,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:29.680
and how amazing they were, and started&nbsp;
listing off all of their great achievements.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:34.320
The things on the list that I heard&nbsp;
her talk about, she had also achieved.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:37.360
Whether it’s on a day to day, week to week,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:42.720
or even just take the opportunity once a&nbsp;
month to remind yourself of all of the things,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.320
over the course of your life&nbsp;
that you have done. And be proud.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:54.720
Our last tip today is to take a moment to&nbsp;
yourself and do something that you enjoy.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:03:00.880
For me, one of my biggest joys is taking a&nbsp;
couple of minutes just to drink a chai latte.&nbsp;

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:05.920
It doesn’t matter where I am. Taking that&nbsp;
couple of minutes to enjoy that hot drink,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:11.040
even the smell of it right now is&nbsp;
making me feel relaxed calm and happy.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.240
There you go guys, that is our final tip&nbsp;
on building resilience, and there are five&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:19.280
different activities there that you can try to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:31.840
implement over the next couple of weeks&nbsp;
and see if it makes a difference to you.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:41.360
If you want to catch up with some of the other&nbsp;
series with things like conflict management,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:46.160
or tips for interviewing then please&nbsp;
take a look and click on the link&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.193
you can see here.
I’ll see you next time!

